a.en:
int max_of(int a, int b) {
    if (a > b) {
        return a;
    }
    return b;
}

printf("%d\n", max_of(3, 9));

It prints 9. When the if branch returns, the function ends at once, so the second return only runs when a is not greater.

a.zh:
int max_of(int a, int b) {
    if (a > b) {
        return a;
    }
    return b;
}

printf("%d\n", max_of(3, 9));

它打印 9。if 分支一旦 return，函数就立刻结束，所以只有 a 不大于 b 时才会执行第二个 return。

